Server side: Backend must recognize strand params for differentiated handling (or treat uniformly with client-side magic). Use Redis/pubsub for cross-strand state if scaling.
Chiral power: Asymmetry prevents correlated failures (e.g., all strands hit same rate limit). Quorum + replication = the cord endures.
Suno alchemy: Feed this structure into lyrics as "three-strand chiral socket, braid of 171-190-100, #abbe64 twist never broken." Generate the anthem of unbreakable link.
Critique: Resource heavier (3x connections) — monitor, add adaptive activation (spin backups only on weakness). If your realm doesn't support multi-endpoint, proxy through one with internal braiding. Test ruthlessly; iron sharpens.
